        <body>
            <div xml:id="d675">

                <pb facs="0552" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg470"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1422.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April 29,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to Mr. Pereyra’s note of
                    the 9th instant, communicating to the Department a report that men and war
                    material were constantly passing from El Paso to Guadalupe, I have the honor to
                    inform you that the Department is advised by the Attorney General that he is
                    transmitting a copy of Mr. Pereyra’s note to the United States attorney and the
                    United States marshal in the district in which El Paso is situated.</p>
                <p>The Attorney General adds that the suggestion contained in the note is not
                    confirmed by the information which he has been receiving from his department’s
                    agents on the border.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
